  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Sagittasine C and M-phase phosphoprotein 8 through a series of target interactions. Sagittasine C is identified as a target of HL-60, which is itself a target of multiple compounds, including Centaurein, (-)-Licarin B, and (2E)-2-Benzylideneoctanal. All of these compounds are linked to the M-phase phosphoprotein 8, indicating a possible pathway through which Sagittasine C may influence this protein. The scores from the three paths are consistent, with a final score of 0.5726 in two of them, suggesting a plausible but not definitive connection. The mechanisms involve the interaction of Sagittasine C with HL-60, which then modulates the activity of M-phase phosphoprotein 8 through various downstream targets. The evidence supports a potential regulatory role of Sagittasine C in the M-phase of the cell cycle, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct interaction and functional significance.",
